<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<Title>TestFramework.Core</Title>
		<Authors>DeadMoon0</Authors>
		<Product>TestFramework</Product>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageTags>Test;UnitTest;IntegrationTest;Framework;Fluent;Timeline</PackageTags>
		<PackageIcon>Icon.png</PackageIcon>
		<Description>The core package of the TestFramework ecosystem for building integration-style and end-to-end test workflows. Provides the timeline engine for steps, events, variables, artifacts, retries, timeouts, and assertions, and serves as the foundation for extension packages like Azure, LocalIO, and Simple.</Description>
		<Version>0.7.0</Version>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Core</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Core.git</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<Copyright>Copyright (c) DeadMoon0 2026</Copyright>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>BREAKING - SetupRun takes output.WriteLine instead of xunit's ITestOutputHelper, and no public member takes optional parameters any more: exceptions, IO declarations, polling results, debugger signals and the graph records use overloads and init properties. BREAKING - an assertion on a variable never set fails, EnsureRanToCompletion fails for a step that never ran, and the blocking PersistentEnvironmentContext constructors are gone; use CreateAsync. New: RunServices.Owned, RunRecord&lt;T&gt;, ArtifactStore.Assign, VariableStore.SetSecretVariable, EnvComponent.StateOf, and a fresh environment per run through IRunScopedEnvironmentFactory, read back from TimelineRun.Environment.</PackageReleaseNotes>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <None Include="..\Modules\TestFramework-Common\Assets\Icon.png">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<!-- Core's own suite, and nobody else. A grant to another package's suite is the same private
		     handshake as a grant to the package: whatever that suite may reach for, every other package's
		     suite may not - and it hides that a surface is missing. Config's suite never used one, and
		     Simple's hand-built the run's pieces until RunContext.Detached existed to hand them over. -->
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>TestFramework.Core.Tests</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" Version="13.0.4" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <None Include="README.md">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
